====== Leetcode 53. Maximum Subarray (27th Feb)=======
Algorithm for finding maximum subarray sum (Kadane’s Algorithm):
Step 1: Initialize a variable cm (current maximum) to 0.
Step 2: Initialize a variable gm (global maximum) to the smallest possible integer value.
Step 3: Traverse each element in the array from left to right.
Step 4: For each element, decide:
•	Either add the current element to the previous sum (cm + current element)
•	Or start a new subarray from the current element
Take the maximum of these two values and store it in cm.
Step 5: Compare cm with gm.
If cm is greater, update gm with cm.
Step 6: Continue this process for all elements in the array.
Step 7: After the loop ends, return gm.
This will be the maximum sum of any continuous subarray.
 
Time Complexity = O(n) 
Space Complexity = O(1)


       ------------------> code <----------------

class Solution {
    public int maxSubArray(int[] nums) {
        int cm=0;
        int gm=Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for(int n:nums){
            cm=Math.max(cm+n,n);
            gm=Math.max(cm,gm);
        }
        return gm;
    }
}
